#### LOW · `PE-IMPORTS-FEW` · `Very few imports`

Confidence low, category anomaly.

`Normal programs import dozens of functions through their C runtime. A near-empty import table suggests packing or position-independent code that finds APIs itself.`

- `imported functions` = `1`
- import `KERNEL32.dll!ExitProcess`

#### INFO · `PE-OVERLAY` · `Data appended after the image`

Confidence high, category anomaly.

`Bytes after the last section are not loaded by Windows. Installers and self-extracting archives keep their payload there; so do droppers.`

- range 0x00000800 (+9 bytes)
- `kind` = `zip`

#### INFO · `PE-PDB-PATH` · `Debug symbols path embedded`

Confidence high, category metadata.

`The linker recorded where the PDB was written. Build paths often reveal user names, project names and directory layouts useful for attribution and for clustering samples from the same build environment.`

